      "description": "Pearl/Ruby Solar Portfolio is a 114 MW portfolio of contracted commercial and industrial distributed-solar assets comprising 134 operating sites across 12 U.S. states. The projects entered service between 2015 and 2018 and sell power under long-term PPAs to commercial, industrial and institutional hosts. Onyx Renewable Partners constructed and financed the assets, sold its sponsor-equity interest to funds managed by Argo Infrastructure Partners in a transaction publicly reported on February 5, 2019, and continued managing the projects. A June 2021 SEC filing lists Pearl/Ruby among Argo's holdings and separately lists Astro Solar. The current GRESB participant page includes Pearl\\ Ruby as a non-listed Americas solar-PV asset, and Argo's July 2026 C&I solar release describes an active expanded platform. No later Pearl/Ruby-level sale or signed pending ownership transfer was identified through August 16, 2026. Public sources do not disclose a legal portfolio suffix, separate official website, headquarters, founding year, named Argo fund, acquisition vehicle, manager-level stake or separate legal closing date.",
